  "body": "Refs #1448. Part of #1448.\n\nDepends on #3324 (the shared mechanism). Do not start before #3324 is merged. The `blocked` label goes when #3324 is closed.\n\n## What happens\n\nDrill, Bore and Thread (mill) cut the holes in the list order. `crates/motion/src/drilling/cycle.rs:40-50` keeps the list order (read, not tested). The user cannot say \"start at this hole\" or \"end at this hole\". Bore has `links` and refuses a pick (`sane.rs:71-87`). Drill and Thread have no `links`.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Start: the hole nearest the start pick is the first hole.\n- Exit: the hole nearest the exit pick is the last hole.\n- The holes between keep a stated order rule. The decision file of #3324 names the rule (for example: the list order, rotated to the start).\n- Probe is not in scope: a probe touch set is not a cut. Its row says so by name.\n\nSeams: `crates/motion/src/drilling/cycle.rs:16` (`drill`), `crates/motion/src/machining2d/bore.rs:249` (`bore`), the Thread arm `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs:2561`. The hole type is `crates/motion/src/drilling/hole.rs:13`.\n\n## Laws a pick must keep (refused by name, never moved)\n\n- The pick is near a hole of the operation, else it is refused.\n- The start hole and the exit hole are not the same hole when the operation has more than one hole, or the decision file states what that means.\n- Break-through and the lathe axial or cross rules keep their refusals (`generate.rs:2330`).\n- The first traverse judges the move to the first hole (`operation/first_traverse.rs:45`).\n\n## Done means\n\n- A pin test for each kind shows the picked first hole and last hole, with golden CL.\n- A pin test shows a pick that is not near a hole refused by name.\n- Undo and redo restore the previous order. MCP `edit_operation` sets the picks.\n- Every shipped drilling golden without a pick is byte-identical.\n\nSafety floor: this changes the posted hole order.\n",
